---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

/* Plain-language and deliberately short. Reviewed-by-a-lawyer status: NOT YET.
   Flagged in the site README — this needs a real read before launch, because
   we collect PII and record calls. */
const updated = 'August 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy — AI Reality Check — SeeSaw Labs"
  description="What we collect when you book an AI Reality Check, why, and how to get rid of it."
>
  <div class="legal">
    <div class="wrap-narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Last updated {updated}</p>
      <h1>Privacy</h1>

      <p class="lede">
        Short version: we collect what we need to prepare for your call and
        build your assessment. We don't sell it, and we don't add you to a
        mailing list you didn't ask for.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>What you type into the form</strong> — your name, work email,
          company, website, industry, role, anything you write about what
          you have already tried, the competitors you name, and who referred
          you if you tell us.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>How you found us</strong> — campaign parameters in the link
          you arrived on, the page you landed on, and the site that referred
          you. We use this to know which channels are worth continuing.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>The call recording and transcript</strong>, if you agree to be
          recorded. We ask at the start of the call. You can say no — the
          assessment just takes an extra day.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Why we collect it</h2>
      <p>
        To decide whether an hour together would be useful, to research your
        situation before the call, and to write the assessment afterwards. The
        answers you give also determine whether we can offer you a slot
        immediately or want to read your answers first.
      </p>

      <h2>Who else sees it</h2>
      <p>
        A small number of processors that run this on our behalf: our scheduler,
        our CRM, our transactional email provider, and our transcription
        service. They're contractually limited to processing it for us. Beyond
        that, nobody — we don't sell or rent it, and we don't share it with
        advertisers.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        Form submissions and assessments stay in our CRM while there's a live
        conversation and for two years after the last contact. Recordings and
        transcripts are deleted once the assessment is delivered and reviewed,
        within 90 days.
      </p>

      <h2>Getting rid of it</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href="mailto:privacy@seesawlabs.com">privacy@seesawlabs.com</a> and
        ask. We'll delete what we hold, tell you what was deleted, and
        confirm within 30 days. You can also ask for a copy of it, or ask us to
        correct it.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        We use privacy-friendly analytics with no cross-site tracking and no
        advertising cookies. Campaign parameters are held in your browser for
        the length of your visit so we can attribute a submission to a source,
        and they're discarded when you close the tab.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        SeeSaw Labs, LLC ·
        <a href="mailto:privacy@seesawlabs.com">privacy@seesawlabs.com</a> ·
        <a href="https://seesawlabs.com">seesawlabs.com</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <style>
    .legal { padding-block: clamp(var(--sp-12), 8vw, var(--sp-20)); }
    .legal h1 {
      font-size: clamp(var(--text-3xl), 5vw, var(--text-5xl));
      margin-bottom: var(--sp-6);
    }
    .legal h2 {
      font-size: var(--text-xl);
      margin: var(--sp-10) 0 var(--sp-3);
    }
    .legal p,
    .legal li {
      color: var(--ink-2);
      font-size: var(--text-md);
      max-width: var(--measure);
    }
    .legal .lede { font-size: var(--text-lg); margin-bottom: var(--sp-4); }
    .legal p { margin-bottom: var(--sp-4); }
    .legal ul { padding-left: var(--sp-5); }
    .legal li { margin-bottom: var(--sp-3); }
    .legal li::marker { color: var(--accent); }
  </style>
</Base>
